# TUI rules

Full guide: [internal/tui/AGENTS.md](mdc:internal/tui/AGENTS.md), [docs/design-language.md](mdc:docs/design-language.md).

- `View` renders state only: no I/O, no mutation (not even scroll offsets). Effects are `tea.Cmd`s returning typed messages. Add a purity test for new panes.
- Semantic tokens from `internal/ui` only. Never color alone: pair with text, prefix or glyph. `NO_COLOR`, `--ascii`, `--accessible` must work; usable at 80x24.
- Every empty, error and waiting state says what happened and the next action. Vim keys per the design-language key map (plan U1). Never advertise a key that is not wired.
- Changed a key? Edit `KeyCatalog` in `cmd/genkeys/main.go`, then `task keys` and commit `docs/keys.md`.
- Masked secrets (`••••`, ASCII `****`) in every frame; extend the `internal/qa` leak sweep for new views.
- Goldens: `go test <pkg> -update`, then read the diff (3 sizes, 3 looks). `task tui:smoke` for an offline pty check.
